  "bounds": "One synthetic simulator whose rows do not react to orders, made-up parameters and 24 days per regime bound what this study can show. Every value is labelled [observed] (read from a log) or [simulated] (an interactive run in the same simulator); nothing here is an off-policy estimate.",
  "claims": "Comparison-specific only. No offline arm is called better or worse than another arm unless the paired 90 % interval excludes zero. An offline arm is called better than an interactive one only against maskable_ppo_regime. No claim about any market or about an estimated regime. Logged data, simulated consequences and interactive results are kept apart in every table. The equal-information comparison covers information only: CQL chooses among three alphas on validation, while maskable_ppo_regime uses set 0, chosen on #102's days under #102's main execution, untuned here with the extra input and the standard execution, and this asymmetry is stated beside every such comparison. Only the pooled interval carries a claim; the per-regime intervals (5 days, mean block 2) are descriptive. The intervals are unadjusted: the seven comparisons have no multiplicity correction, which is stated with them.",
